Z||000011||Screwie||10-26-2001||02:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Blondie88:<BR><B>But I looked up the word fiero and found that in French and Dutch it means proud, and if you go from french to german or finnish or something in means trots!  Sunglass guy wasn't sure you guys would know.  I told him that you would! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well actually, Fiero is not a Dutch word. But 'fier' is, and that means 'proud'. But the other Dutch word for 'proud' is 'trots'. In French it's also 'fier' and not Fiero. In German it actually is 'stolz'.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Dunno about finnish though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Voytek||10-26-2001||02:48 PM||||It's definitely the 'proud' or 'very proud' thing.  It says that in the Fiero book so it MUST be true.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
